.Dd 2026-05-30
.Dt NOMAD-CLEAN 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm nomad-clean
.Nd reclaim disk space from install detritus, safely
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm nomad clean
.Op Fl -apply
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm nomad clean
frees disk space by removing artifacts left behind by installs and partial
downloads, without touching any data or state you want to keep.
It removes
.Pa /tmp/nomad-*.log
files, the
.Pa compose.yaml.bak
backup from the amd64 fallback path, quarantined partial ZIMs under
.Pa $NOMAD_DATA_ROOT/storage/zim-inprogress ,
dangling Docker images, the Docker builder cache, and stopped
admin-spawned content containers.
.Pp
It never touches Ollama models, downloaded ZIMs, the mysql or redis data,
the secrets file, the LaunchAgents, or any container that is currently
running.
.Pp
By default
.Nm nomad clean
is a dry run: it reports what it would remove and an estimate of the space
involved.
Pass
.Fl -apply
to actually perform the cleanup.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -apply
Perform the cleanup rather than only reporting it.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic nomad clean
Show what would be cleaned, without removing anything.
.It Ic nomad clean --apply
Remove the detritus and report the space freed.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr nomad 1 ,
.Xr nomad-fix-kiwix 1 ,
.Xr nomad-uninstall 1
